\f0\fs24 \cf0 The longs drugs brand revival project is a comprehensive project that established new guidelines for the brand, modernized the typography, and expanded the working color palette of for the brand in order to reshape it\'92s local identity from an old traditional stable of Hawaii, to a modern staple of Hawaii that has stood the test of time for it\'92s community.\
\
I was asked by CVS Health to modernize the Longs Drugs brand and set it up for a multi-layered transition that would give the brand the ability to expand with store products, a lively social media and website presence and engaging physical and digital banners.\
\
I wanted to keep true to the roots of the brand as much as possible. That meant prioritizing the longs drugs red. What is also meant was keeping the iconic yellow, from the printed circular the islands are used to seeing associated with the brand and using that in a way that wouldn\'92t be too harsh. In the end, came to the conclusion that have one primary color, the red and two secondary colors would be the best start. The secondary colors were a rich yellow, to stay true to the history of longs and a navy blue in order to maintain flexibility with it\'92s parent company CVS Health and evoke trust and stability to the audience. Afterwards I worked on expanding a working color palette as tertiary colors, that would not only work well with the main 3 colors, but would also be able to add energy and life to creative and still be recognizable as one brand. This would also allow the brand to create distinct creative for events, seasons, and campaigns while not appearing disconnected from it\'92s core brand.\
\
The outcome has been multi layered. A quickly maturing website that is outpacing local competitors and with its relative size competition well against national competitors. A growing and engaging social media presence and a solid, fun, and recognizable physical presence across the islands of Hawaii.}